From: Arvind Yadav <arvind.yadav.cs@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/xe/vm: Handle NULL resource in xe_vm_snapshot_capture()

xe_vm_snapshot_capture() dereferences bo->ttm.resource unconditionally
when recording the memory region of a mapped bo. A purged bo has no
resource, so this is a NULL pointer dereference.

xe_ttm_bo_purge() purges with an empty ttm_placement, which makes
ttm_bo_validate() take the ttm_bo_pipeline_gutting() path. That frees the
resource through ttm_resource_free(), which sets bo->ttm.resource to NULL.

The purged bo stays mapped in the VM by design: xe_vm_populate_validate()
skips re-populating it and the rebind maps scratch pages instead, with
xelp_pte_encode_bo() setting XE_PTE_NULL for a purged bo on a scratch VM.
The VMA is never removed, so it is still walked by the devcoredump handler.

If a GPU hang then triggers a devcoredump on a VM holding such a bo, the
switch on bo->ttm.resource->mem_type oopses. Userspace only needs
madvise(DONTNEED) on a mapped bo and a subsequent hang, so an unprivileged
process can use this for a denial of service.

Record -ENODATA for a bo with no resource instead. This matches how the
existing fallback branch reports an unusable mapping, and both consumers
already handle it: xe_vm_snapshot_capture_delayed() skips entries whose
data is an error pointer, and xe_vm_snapshot_print() prints the error and
moves on. -1 is already the established uapi_mem_region sentinel for "no
region" and xe_vm_snapshot_print() special-cases it.

Read the resource once into a local so the NULL test and the mem_type
access cannot see different values.

This deliberately does not take the bo reservation. Capture runs inside the
dma_fence_begin_signalling() section opened by devcoredump_snapshot() and
holds vm->snap_mutex, which is itself taken under the reservation on the
gpuva insert/remove paths, so only a trylock would be legal. A trylock is
not worth it here: bos bound to a VM share the VM reservation, so a single
contended resv would blank the memory region for every bo in the dump,
while the race it would close requires TTM eviction or swapout to purge
that exact bo within the few instructions between the load and the
dereference. Stale data in a coredump is acceptable; the deterministic
NULL dereference fixed here is not.

Signed-off-by: Arvind Yadav <arvind.yadav.cs@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
index 9e0176861c..fa3415b2c6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
@@ -4513,6 +4513,7 @@ struct xe_vm_snapshot *xe_vm_snapshot_capture(struct xe_vm *vm)
 		struct xe_vma *vma = gpuva_to_vma(gpuva);
 		struct xe_bo *bo = vma->gpuva.gem.obj ?
 			gem_to_xe_bo(vma->gpuva.gem.obj) : NULL;
+		struct ttm_resource *res = bo ? bo->ttm.resource : NULL;
 
 		if (!(gpuva->flags & XE_VMA_DUMPABLE))
 			continue;
@@ -4522,11 +4523,20 @@ struct xe_vm_snapshot *xe_vm_snapshot_capture(struct xe_vm *vm)
 		snap->snap[i].flags = xe_vma_read_only(vma) ?
 			XE_VM_SNAP_FLAG_READ_ONLY : 0;
 		snap->snap[i].pat_index = vma->attr.pat_index;
-		if (bo) {
+		if (bo && !res) {
+			/*
+			 * A purged bo has had its resource freed, so there is
+			 * nothing to capture. Record the error instead of
+			 * dereferencing a NULL resource; xe_bo_read() would
+			 * fail with -ENODATA for this bo anyway.
+			 */
+			snap->snap[i].data = ERR_PTR(-ENODATA);
+			snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = -1;
+		} else if (bo) {
 			snap->snap[i].cpu_caching = bo->cpu_caching;
 			snap->snap[i].bo = xe_bo_get(bo);
 			snap->snap[i].bo_ofs = xe_vma_bo_offset(vma);
-			switch (bo->ttm.resource->mem_type) {
+			switch (res->mem_type) {
 			case XE_PL_SYSTEM:
 			case XE_PL_TT:
 				snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 0;
